    "adapt": "A hostless open-ground camp on the north outpost site: no building, so the kit never turns past the dossier yaw. Every row rests on the probed ground (`--terrain`). The six `outpost-spot-*` rows have no prefab: they are the named spots for the crate (#4223), chalk board (GA-O3), buyer, quartermaster and the two gate guards (#4519); a consumer reads their offset and yaw. The gate is a 4 m opening in the sandbag line facing the kit's -x side. Rows are rigid: shift, never stretch."
